<p>The United States is sending more than 2,000 Marines and at least one amphibious assault ship from Japan to the Middle East as the conflict with Iran nears a third week. Reports tied the move to forces based in Japan, with SCMP identifying the Okinawa-based 31st Marine Expeditionary Unit and USS Tripoli as part of the deployment. The move is another step up in US involvement. President Trump has vowed to intensify the campaign, and Iran’s response to sustained strikes has proved tougher than administration officials expected.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kjRSU7m2S4rGKBPFShUD1AtM8v8ZFMy6tizSZ46sLtPHo0JKsONcx3Ht1wtplb4qr-Ai0UdbvoCC0edobJkG7oTx_r9rSuVh3aE0gt_Kc7ybLKJV-V5Eh7AfJH2O2VwcQu6HPsf1GyDqU2nA4hp8VbrSJwKLEnXvt5tz6mLr4uDfa-9qZBfYdizIYBx9LZLmDz_SkcEjpLSRUohtBCoGZ3TOLZRq6PVuzIA' alt='Navy ships in Nagasaki, Japan, in 2023.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Troop count gap: PBS put the deployment at around 2,500 Marines, while other outlets cited more than 2,000, showing that public accounts were still relying on approximate totals.</li><li>Package still being pieced together: SCMP specifically named the 31st Marine Expeditionary Unit and USS Tripoli, while BBC described the reinforcement more broadly as coming from an amphibious ready group based in Japan. That suggests officials had not publicly laid out the full force package in one place.</li><li>Mission still unspecified: PBS said the Marines’ mission was not yet clear, so the Pentagon is moving additional forces before publicly defining exactly how commanders plan to use them.</li><li>Operational backdrop: The Pentagon said strikes had hit more than 15,000 targets in Iran over nearly two weeks, putting the new deployment alongside an already large and sustained campaign.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US officials: The New York Times reported that Iran remained more resilient than officials expected even after days of aerial bombardment and long-range artillery strikes, helping explain the push to send additional forces. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/13/world/middleeast/us-marines-warships-middle-east.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>PBS: PBS said the Marines’ mission was not yet clear, but described the move as a marked increase in US forces in the region. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/more-marines-heading-to-middle-east-as-u-s-continues-relentless-strikes-on-iran'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>US military officials: An official told CBS, as cited by the BBC, that the reinforcements were coming from an amphibious ready group usually based in Japan, pointing to a redeployment of existing forward forces rather than a permanent basing change. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq8gj9n12g8o'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3346580/us-moves-2000-marines-japan-middle-east-iran-war-intensifies'>US moves 2,000 Marines from Japan to Middle East as Iran war intensifies</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq8gj9n12g8o'>More US Marines and warships to be moved to Middle East, reports say</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/more-marines-heading-to-middle-east-as-u-s-continues-relentless-strikes-on-iran'>More Marines heading to Middle East as U.S. continues relentless strikes on Iran</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/13/world/middleeast/us-marines-warships-middle-east.html'>More Marines and Warships Being Sent to Middle East, U.S. Officials Say</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1rsysfa/panicked_pentagon_sends_land_invasion_force_to/'>Panicked Pentagon Sends Land Invasion Force to Middle East: ‘As many as 5,000 additional U.S. Marines are heading for the Middle East in a possible escalation of Donald Trump&#x27;s war on Iran’</a> - reddit.com</li></ul>